s is one of the most unique  looking animated films that I've seen it  uses a whole mixture of different  mediums to create this kaleidoscope of  colors and this mess of magic it's all  about growing up and trying to overcome  your issues and the kind of  relationships and archetypes that you  face in high school beyond that though  it is really really funny  where legs are caught into the foot case  I gotta amputate Jude just lift the  bookcase oh yeah okay I had a great time  watching my entire high school sinking  into the sea when I started at Fantastic  Fest last year it's coming out in  limited theaters from this weekend if  you can't see it now note down this  title for when it comes out on video on  demand  and Truman is another film coming out in  limited theaters this weekend it is a  Spanish Argentine drama about the power  of friendship this looks at two male  friends who have been lifelong buddies  they reconnect after many many years  just as one of them has been diagnosed  with cancer and he decides not to do  anything about it  the Truman in the title is the dog  Truman who he wants to read home before  you passes away  but it is doing better than we have a  girl William good nobody here but it's a  tough subject matter but it's done  without sentimentality I really liked  that I also liked how it showed male  friendships and male bonding in a  different way Truman came out in  theaters in New York last week it's  coming out in Los Angeles this weekend  and then hopefully other places after  that  [Music]  and just before I go I want to mention  two inspiring films based on true  stories both out on Fandango now or  video-on-demand this weekend  the first is hidden figures this is  about three african-american women who  were instrumental in the NASA space  program in the 60s deals with racism and  sexism but heartwarming at the same time  and overall it's a crowd-pleasing movie  made a lot of money at the box office  and I'm so glad for that because it  tells such a great story and it has a  cast that are wonderful in their roles  taraji P Henson Janelle Monae and  Octavia Spencer if you missed it at the  theater if you want to watch it again  you can see it on Fandango now from  April 14 let me ask you if you are white  mane would you wish to be an engineer I  wouldn't have to and another of my  favorites from last year was lion this  is based on a true story of a young  Indian boy who gets lost from his home  becomes adopted by an Australian family  and then uses Google Maps to try to  track down his old village it serves Dev  Patel who does a great Australian accent  and also Rooney Mara and Nicole Kidman  in a very heartbreaking performance lion  will definitely make you cry it'll make  you cheer it'll make you smile and you  can see it on Fandango now from April 14  every night I imagine that I'm walking  those streets home and I know every  single step of the way  lots to choose from this weekend in  theaters you can see Norman the moderate  rise and tragic fall of a New York fixer  or my entire high school sinking into  the sea or Truman or you can stay at  home and watch hidden figures or lions  and just as I wrap up I want to quickly  put out there if you're loving the saw  Ragnarok trailer and you haven't seen  Taika Waititi the director these other  films and make sure you check out hunt  for the world of or eagle versus shark  or boy or what we do in the shadows  because that will showcase the great  humor that we've started to see from  that trailer don't forget to let me know  which indie films you've been loving  lately and if you've managed to catch  any of my suggestions I'm Alisha Malone  you can find me on Twitter at least  Malone and I'll see you soon  [Music]

